input.body:
`packs/claudinite-tasks/migrations/2026-09-05-task-cadence-terms/migration.mjs` gates itself on the member's mount understanding the cadence vocabulary, by content:

```js
const CALENDAR = 'packs/claudinite-tasks/calendar.mjs';
const twoRoot = async (read, file) => (await read(`.claudinite/shared/${file}`)) ?? (await read(file));
const mountReadsBothFields = async (read) => {
  const calendar = await twoRoot(read, CALENDAR);
  …
  return Boolean(calendar) && calendar.includes('cadenceTermFor') && …;
};
```

`packs/claudinite-tasks/calendar.mjs` was moved to `packs/claudinite-tasks/src/contract/calendar.mjs` by #1890 (`1b639e3`, 2026-09-14) with no shim left at the old path. Both arms of the two-root probe therefore miss, `appliesTo` returns false, and — since an unreadable mount reads as "not capable" by design — the record has been silently inert ever since.

**What that costs.** The record is what folds a member's own `frequency` into `preconditions` on the nightly update. It applied for the eight nights between #1733 merging (2026-09-06) and the move; after that, a member converging for the first time has not had its rewrite. #1732 has now closed the contract's door, so such a member's task declaration is rejected outright rather than read — the break the record existed to prevent.

**Why not fixed in #1732's own pull request (#2138).** Repointing the probe makes a codemod start writing to members' own files across the fleet. That is a delivery change with its own blast radius, and #1732's automerge policy was predicted from the door-removal diff; widening it to carry this would land a fleet-wide write under a policy written for something else.

## What to do

- [ ] Repoint `CALENDAR` at `packs/claudinite-tasks/src/contract/calendar.mjs`, and re-check `SCHEMA` (`packs/claudinite-tasks/task.schema.json`) survived the same move — it did, but confirm rather than assume.
- [ ] Re-check the record's `version: '60906.9'` gate still sits above the installed version of the members that never got the rewrite, and below the number since cut — `claudinite-tasks` is at `60918.2`, so a member that last converged before `60906.9` still applies it and one past it does not.
- [ ] Pin the probe against the real tree, so the next layout change cannot silently re-inert it: a path pattern that matches nothing reads as live.
- [ ] Sweep every other migration record for a literal pack path that the `src/<role>/` move (#1890) invalidated — this class of bug is silent by construction.

_Filed by the Claudinite task `claudinite-tasks/implement-request`, running as work item missingbulb/Claudinite#1732 — no person asked for this issue._

